<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale %>">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Toishi Note" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Toishi Note">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%# UI copy that a Stimulus controller needs at runtime (a toast
        message, a client-side validation error) — not note content, never
        the request/response strings Rails already renders server-side.
        See app/javascript/lib/translations.js. %>
    <meta name="translations" content="<%= t("js").to_json %>">

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">

    <%# :app bulk-includes every plain .css file under app/assets/**/*.css
        (Propshaft's stylesheet_link_tag override) — this is how
        app/assets/stylesheets/katex/katex.min.css (vendored, not
        CDN-loaded — see docs/engineering/asset-strategy.md) reaches the
        page with no separate tag needed. KaTeX, Mermaid, and
        highlight.js are all loaded as npm imports from
        lib/markdown_renderer.js instead of CDN <script> tags: nothing
        in this app's runtime path is fetched from a third party. %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>

    <%= javascript_include_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload", type: "module" %>
  </head>

  <body data-controller="navigation">
    <%= yield %>

    <div class="toast-container position-fixed top-0 end-0 p-3" style="z-index: 1090;" data-controller="toast">
      <div class="toast align-items-center text-bg-dark border-0" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-toast-target="toast" data-action="toast:show@window->toast#show">
        <div class="d-flex">
          <div class="toast-body" data-toast-target="body"></div>
          <button type="button" class="btn-close btn-close-white me-2 m-auto" data-bs-dismiss="toast" aria-label="Close"></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Server-side confirmation for a redirect-driven action (notebook/
        folder/note create, rename, delete — see NotebooksController,
        FoldersController, NotesController) rides across the redirect as
        flash[:toast], then this bridges it into the same toast the rest
        of the app already uses for JS-driven confirmations (see
        app/javascript/controllers/toast_controller.js). Deliberately a
        separate flash key from :notice/:alert, which sessions/passwords
        views already render inline themselves — using :toast here avoids
        double-displaying those. Must come after the toast-container above
        — Stimulus connects controllers in document order, and this
        controller dispatches toast:show synchronously from connect(), so
        the toast controller's own connect() (which wires up its
        toast:show listener) needs to have already run. %>
    <% if flash[:toast].present? %>
      <div data-controller="flash-toast" data-flash-toast-message-value="<%= flash[:toast] %>"></div>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>